#chapter-head("Chapter 06", "Sabotage in Biotechnica Flats", "BADLANDS // BIOTECHNICA FLATS SERVICE YARD · 22:26")

#prose-lead("M")[isty’s call came through once the southern repeater triangulation locked: the desert convoy carrying Lucía and Mateo had stopped once more at an abandoned service yard in Biotechnica Flats before disappearing toward Solís’s subterranean bunker.]

V straddled Scorpion’s weathered Apollo and throttled hard down the long wet straightaways south of Night City, leaving the skyline’s neon haze behind for lonely sodium highway lamps, scrub brush, and the endless rustle of desert wind. Out beyond the protein farms, beneath twin service lights, stood an old convoy trailer and glowing red floodlamps—and waiting in the dirt around it was a Pale Chorus cleanup crew still guarding the drop.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_12_badlands_ride.jpg",
  "FIG. 12 // OUTBOUND FOR BIOTECHNICA FLATS",
  "Following Viktor and Misty's triangulated relay beacons, V rides south into the Badlands night toward the Pale Chorus convoy drop.",
)

No passphrases worked out here in the red dirt. _Carnage_ boomed twice across the service yard while V flanked past green-lit cryo cables snaking along the mud, trading buckshot bursts until the last nocturnal sentry dropped beside the convoy trailer.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_13_flats_ambush.jpg",
  "FIG. 13 // CONVOY DROP SKIRMISH",
  "V clears the Pale Chorus cleanup squad defending the deserted Biotechnica Flats service yard where Lucía's cryo-pod was unsealed.",
)

Quiet returned to the flats, broken only by the cooling tick of spent brass and the low hum of an active microwave relay. Three fragments told the entire story of what had happened here two nights ago: first, an open cryo transfer pod stamped `Subject L-14 — Lucía Reyes`, emptied alongside fresh calibration vials labeled `NOX-9B`; second, resting in the dust beside another stained *Moon* card, the shattered Northside dock identification badge of *Mateo (M-09)* with clipped cryo-power lines splayed beside him.

Mateo hadn't died quietly in a tank. He had severed the convoy’s cryogenic umbilicals out in the desert trying to buy Lucía a window to run—and Helena Solís had executed him right on the gravel and wiped his ledger.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_14_flats_relay.jpg",
  "FIG. 14 // TELEMETRY HANDSHAKE",
  "A glowing cryo-relay unit in the service yard retains the final directional handshake: one kilometer northeast, beneath Biotechnica's decommissioned geothermal plant.",
)

The third artifact—a battered relay box resting atop a crate—still cached the convoy’s final destination handshake: *one kilometer northeast, buried beneath Biotechnica’s abandoned geothermal power station.*

#forensic-dossier(
  "CODEX // CV-SHARD-A2-FLATS",
  "Biotechnica Flats Convoy Drop — Forensic Record",
  [
    - *Cryo-Pod L-14:* Held Lucía Reyes during desert transit alongside NOX-9B calibration samples.\
    - *Subject M-09 (Mateo):* Cut the pod's cryo power lines in an effort to free Lucía; Helena Solís executed him beside the service yard and purged his medical ledger.\
    - *Microwave Relay:* Locks onto a subterranean thermal sink beneath Biotechnica's decommissioned geothermal station.
  ],
)

#chapter-head("Chapter 07", "Two Sublevels Beneath the Ash", "BADLANDS // GEOTHERMAL PLANT & DIALYSIS WING · 23:23")

#prose-lead("B")[ehind corrugated perimeter walls and stacked cargo containers, Biotechnica’s old geothermal plant rose out of the dark like a sleeping foundry—guarded outside by Pale Chorus riflemen and another `365 nm` ultraviolet tower.]

This time V knew the choreography by heart: shatter the UV housing, blind the night-adapted sentries before their dermal chrome could stitch bullet holes shut, and sweep the yard clean. Waiting beside the heavy armored hatch at the edge of the courtyard—alive, exhausted, wearing her studded collar, sleeveless vest, and red forearm wraps—stood *Lucía Reyes*.

For a second she stared through the dark as if expecting another hallucination from withdrawal. Then recognition hit.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_15_lucia_bunker.jpg",
  "FIG. 15 // GEOTHERMAL PLANT PERIMETER",
  "Alive beneath the desert night, Lucía Reyes meets V beside the bunker access hatch and confirms NOX-9B synthesis has reached 98 percent below.",
)

#dialogue-block("Lucía Reyes", "V? I knew Misty would read the two notches on The Moon card! I thought nobody would ever track me out this far past Watson.")
#dialogue-block("V", "Misty tore half of Watson apart to find you, Lucía. You're clear for now—tell me everything happening down in that bunker.")

Lucía’s voice steadied when speaking of Mateo. He had been the first to realize their clinic wasn't curing anyone—only engineering lifelong chemical dependency—and he died cutting the cryo lines so she might bolt. Worse still was what waited down the stairwell: Dr. Helena Solís’s lower bioreactor was already at *ninety-eight percent synthesis* on porphyrin-free `NOX-9B`. Once it finished, `365 nm` ultraviolet light would never burn them again, and Solís had already ordered Misty’s Esoterica erased.

V stationed Lucía safely behind the outer perimeter barrier and dropped down into the geothermal plant’s subterranean gut.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_16_sub1_dialysis.jpg",
  "FIG. 16 // SUBLEVEL -1 · DIALYSIS WING",
  "Inside the crimson-lit underground wing, V purges the access seal relay, overloads the floor's 365 nm UV rig, and cuts through Pale Chorus stalkers.",
)

*Sublevel -1 (The Dialysis Wing)* smelled of iron, bleach, and stale incense. V bypassed the cryogenic access seal relay (`1/4`), sprinted straight across blood-slick tile under automatic fire to overload the hall’s `365 nm` UV emitter (`2/4`), hunted down the remaining stalkers and blood-blades in the violet glare (`3/4`), and unlocked the stairwell descent hatch into *Sublevel -2: The Crimson Sanctum* (`4/4`).

Down in the deeper corridor, the air grew thick and strangely resonant—a sub-audible carrier hum vibrating behind V’s Kiroshi temple plates as ultraviolet floodlamps strobed violet fog off steel pipes and strip curtains. One more UV overload shattered the sanctum vanguard’s advantage before V pushed past the plastic curtains into the inner reactor terrace: *Studio NOX-9B*.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_17_sub2_uv_blast.jpg",
  "FIG. 17 // SUBLEVEL -2 · CORRIDOR UV OVERLOAD",
  "Blinding 365 nm ultraviolet discharge floods the lower sanctum corridor, stripping Pale Chorus vanguard chrome of nocturnal regeneration.",
)

#chapter-head("Chapter 08", "The Cantor and the Second Serum", "STUDIO NOX-9B // SUBLEVEL -2 CORE · 22:19")

#prose-lead("I")[nside the shuttered glass and fluorescent twilight of Studio NOX-9B, motionless white mannequins stood like silent parishioners beside blood-stained examination mats and glowing red server consoles.]

Waiting in the center of the terrace—immaculate in a black tailored suit trimmed with crimson lapels, sleek wraparound visor hiding her eyes, calm as a boardroom executive—stood *Dr. Helena Solís*. Even surrounded by armed honor guards, she didn't reach for a weapon at first. She raised one gloved hand with measured, almost clinical poise.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_18_solis_confront.jpg",
  "FIG. 18 // STUDIO NOX-9B · CONFRONTATION",
  "Flanked by honor guards and silent mannequins, Dr. Helena Solís (‘The Cantor’) defends The Pale Chorus as nocturnal salvation for Watson's discarded.",
)

#dialogue-block("Dr. Helena Solís", "So you're Misty Olszewski's hound. I expected Biotechnica clean-up or Valdés's panic, not someone still chasing sentimental rescues.")
#dialogue-block("V", "Valdés built NOX-9 to heal damaged lungs, Solís. You twisted it into a cult and executed Mateo when he tried to walk.")
#dialogue-block("Dr. Helena Solís", "Biotechnica left Watson workers choking because they couldn't afford chrome. I gave them regeneration and belonging in the dark. Mateo broke our oath and endangered everyone.")

Nothing in her voice cracked. Not when V pressed her on _NOX-9B_—which Solís coolly confirmed eliminated `365 nm` phototoxicity entirely, returning sovereignty over sunlight to whoever controlled the formula—and not when V demanded why Esoterica had been marked _Nexus of Silence_. Lucía’s notched Tarot cards proved Misty’s shop still anchored initiates to the world outside the Chorus; to descend from the tower, Solís reasoned, one closed every door behind.

Three choices hung in the fluorescent air: burn the core to ash, strike a dirty truce to spare Watson, or seize the purified formula alive so Dr. Valdés and Viktor could actually finish what Valdés started six years ago. V didn't blink.

#dialogue-block("V", "You're done trading in other people's veins, Solís. I'm taking NOX-9B intact to Valdés and walking Lucía out of here tonight.")
#dialogue-block("Dr. Helena Solís", "Then burn beneath the Pale Chorus! Lock the reactor terrace and keep them off that core!")

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_19_solis_battle.jpg",
  "FIG. 19 // CLIMAX IN STUDIO NOX-9B",
  "Under a triggered 365 nm UV overload, Dr. Helena Solís and her Phase II reinforcement stalkers ignite with phototoxic feedback.",
)

The terrace erupted. Solís’s honor blades surged forward while Phase II reinforcement stalkers breached the doorway, their chrome stitching wounds in real time until V smashed the chamber’s tripod UV rig behind the console. Violet arc light flooded the Venetian blinds; Solís’s visor flared with thermal sparks as Copperhead rounds tore through her barrier until the Cantor finally collapsed beside the core terminal.

V’s jack clicked cleanly into the NOX-9B bioreactor console. Green telemetry scrolled past: `98% -> 100% PURIFIED SYNTHESIS EXTRACTED & ENCRYPTED`.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_20_nox9b_core.jpg",
  "FIG. 20 // ENDING A · NOX-9B SECURED",
  "With the chamber cleared and Solís defeated, V downloads and encrypts the purified NOX-9B formula for Dr. Valdés and Viktor before evacuating.",
)

#dialogue-block("V", "Purified NOX-9B synthesis pulled and encrypted for Valdés and Misty. Time to bring Lucía home to Watson.")

Minutes later, the emergency extraction shaft spat V and Lucía back into cool Badlands midnight. The war beneath the ash was over.
